---
// src/pages/about.astro — about, disclosure, privacy
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About, disclosure & privacy · ai4you.site">
  <div class="about wrap--narrow wrap">
    <span class="kicker">Who we are</span>
    <h1>About, disclosure &amp; privacy.</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <section id="about">
        <h2>What this is</h2>
        <p>
          ai4you.site is an independent briefing on artificial intelligence: model releases, pricing
          changes, industry shocks and the occasional deep dive — every story linked to its primary
          source. We started it because the AI news cycle went from quarterly to weekly, and most
          coverage is either hype or panic. We'd rather be the calm one.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are not owned by, funded by, or affiliated with any AI lab. The site is
          reader-supported: when you subscribe to a tool through one of our labeled links, the
          vendor pays us a commission.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="disclosure">
        <h2>Affiliate disclosure</h2>
        <p>
          Some links on ai4you.site are affiliate links. If you click one and sign up or buy
          something, we may receive a commission from the vendor. <strong>You never pay more</strong>
          for using our links — in a few cases you may pay less, if we can negotiate a discount.
        </p>
        <p>
          Here is the part most sites bury: <strong>commissions never decide what we publish.</strong>
          Tools get on the shelf because we'd recommend them anyway; plenty of tools we recommend
          have no affiliate program at all, and those links are marked as plain. Every affiliate
          link is disclosed next to where it appears and tagged <code>rel="sponsored"</code> for
          search engines.
        </p>
        <p>
          This disclosure follows the U.S. FTC's Guides Concerning the Use of Endorsements and
          Testimonials in Advertising (16 CFR Part 255), which require that material connections
          between reviewers and vendors be clearly and conspicuously disclosed. As a small site we
          treat the FTC's own guidance — clear, unavoidable, near the link — as the standard
          everywhere on the site, not just on this page.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="standards">
        <h2>Editorial standards</h2>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li><span class="n">1</span><span><b>Sourced or it didn't happen.</b> Every news item links to a primary source or established outlet. No anonymous "reports say" without a link.</span></li>
          <li><span class="n">2</span><span><b>Dates on everything.</b> AI claims rot fast; every story carries its publication date and we correct visibly when we're wrong.</span></li>
          <li><span class="n">3</span><span><b>No pay-to-play.</b> Vendors cannot buy coverage, rankings or placement. Sponsored content, if we ever run it, will be labeled in the headline, not the footer.</span></li>
          <li><span class="n">4</span><span><b>Numbers get context.</b> Benchmarks mean little without prices, latency and real workflows. We say so when a "record" is vendor-measured.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="privacy">
        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p><strong>The short version: this site does not track you.</strong> No accounts for readers, no advertising cookies, no analytics scripts as of launch. No personal information is collected, sold, or shared, because none is collected at all.</p>
        <p><strong>Newsletter.</strong> If you subscribe, we receive your email address and use it only to send the newsletter. Every issue contains a one-click unsubscribe. We never sell or share the list beyond the email service that delivers it.</p>
        <p><strong>Click counts.</strong> When you open an affiliate link, the click is counted (an anonymous counter row — no profile, no identifier). The affiliate vendor's own privacy policy applies from that moment.</p>
        <p><strong>Admin.</strong> The link dashboard is restricted to the site operator; readers have no accounts and nothing to log into.</p>
        <p>Questions about anything on this page: write to <strong>hello [at] ai4you [dot] site</strong>. This policy isn't legal advice and we're not lawyers — for your own projects, get real counsel.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
